{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Sorry I'm late. Tram was a shocker.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): No worries. Warm arvo out there.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (NURSE): Cuff's going on now. My sister missed her own ultrasound last Thursday, the Monash was a car park.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thanks. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (PATIENT): Pain. Right side. Up here.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Up under the ribs on the right. When did it start?",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (PATIENT): umm.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (PATIENT): Three months.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Three months. Does it follow certain meals, or—",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): Fatty.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Fatty meals. How long does a spell last before it—",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (PATIENT): Hours.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hours, right. Any vomiting?",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (PATIENT): Once.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Once only. Has it come back?",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): And any fever with these?",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (PATIENT): After chips.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Chips, I'll add that to the fatty food. I meant fever. Any temperature?",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): No temperature. Have you taken anything?",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (PATIENT): Milanta.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mylanta, from the chemist. How many?",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (PATIENT): Two tablets. When it starts.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Two tablets when it starts. Does it help?",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (PATIENT): Bit.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me read that back. Three months of pain under the right ribs, after fatty meals and chips, each spell lasts hours, you vomited once and not since, no fever, and two Mylanta tablets take the edge off.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Gallbladder problems in the family?",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (PATIENT): Mum. Surgery.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Your mum had gallbladder surgery. After a fatty meal the gallbladder squeezes, and if a stone is sitting in the outlet that squeeze can hurt for hours.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (NURSE): Blood pressure is one twenty-eight over seventy-eight. Pulse seventy-six.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ta. I'll have a feel. Err, tender under the right ribs. No guarding, and the belly is soft.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (PATIENT): Ow.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry. Any yellow in the eyes, or pale stools?",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): And a quick chest check. Any cough or trouble getting your breath?",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): I reckon this is biliary colic, most likely stones, but that's provisional till the scan.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll book bloods, liver tests and a full blood count, plus an ultrasound of the tummy. Ease off the fatty food, keep the two Mylanta tablets when it starts, and come back in two weeks for the results."
 ],
